  <section>
    <h2>Overview</h2>
    <p>Above All Greenery is a Maine medical cannabis operator that built a large and sophisticated indoor cultivation operation in 2020 and now distributes through at least two storefront locations. The original dispensary is in West Newfield, ME. The Fryeburg location, marketed as Above All Greenery North, extends the same quality and care commitment to the western Maine corridor along Route 302.</p>
    <p>All cannabis sold at Above All Greenery is grown in-house. The operator markets this as a quality differentiator: pesticide-free product, single-source supply chain, and state-accredited lab testing on every batch. For medical patients who prioritize clean, consistent, traceable medicine, this is the operator's primary value proposition.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Fryeburg (Above All Greenery North)</h2>
    <p><strong>Address:</strong> 48 Fair Street, Unit 4, Fryeburg, ME 04037<br>
    <strong>Hours (verify before visiting):</strong> Monday closed · Tuesday–Friday 10am–6pm · Saturday 10am–5pm · Sunday 9am–5pm</p>
    <p>The Fryeburg location serves the western Maine medical community, including Fryeburg proper, Conway / North Conway NH (just across the border), Brownfield, Denmark, Lovell, and Stow. NH residents with a valid Maine medical card (or a reciprocity state card) can purchase at the Fryeburg location. The dispensary is also a short drive from the White Mountain National Forest corridor.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Product Standard</h2>
    <p>Above All Greenery's product standard is built around three commitments:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>In-house cultivation.</strong> Every product on the menu comes from the operator's own indoor grow. There is no white-labeling or third-party sourcing.</li>
      <li><strong>Pesticide-free cultivation.</strong> The operator's site explicitly states products are "pesticide-free and natural." Maine requires pesticide testing on the regulatory panel; Above All Greenery's commitment is to keep that panel clean rather than just meet the threshold.</li>
      <li><strong>State-accredited lab testing.</strong> All products are tested by OCP-certified Maine labs. The four OCP-licensed testing labs in Maine are CATLab (Eliot), MCR Labs (Gardiner), Nelson Analytical (Kennebunk), and Nova Analytic Labs (Windham).</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Service Area</h2>
    <p>The Fryeburg location serves the western Maine and southern New Hampshire medical corridor:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Fryeburg</strong> (in town) — 5 min</li>
      <li><strong>Conway / North Conway, NH</strong> — 20-25 min south</li>
      <li><strong>Brownfield / Denmark</strong> — 10-15 min</li>
      <li><strong>Lovell / Stow</strong> — 15-20 min</li>
      <li><strong>Cornish / Hiram</strong> — 15-20 min</li>
      <li><strong>Bridgton</strong> — 15-20 min east</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Patients closer to Portland, Biddeford, or the southern Maine corridor should check the operator's West Newfield location or other Maine medical dispensaries for a closer option.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>How to Verify Before You Go</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Official site:</strong> <a href="https://aboveallgreenery.net/">aboveallgreenery.net</a></li>
      <li><strong>Fryeburg guide:</strong> <a href="/guides/fryeburg-dispensary-guide">Town-level overview of Fryeburg dispensaries</a></li>
    </ul>
    <p>Bring your Maine MMMP card and a valid government photo ID. Out-of-state medical patients from a reciprocity state should call ahead to confirm acceptance.</p>
  </section>

